are connected through that room.

202
00:11:08,280 --> 00:11:11,580
Let's go see Jodie and Nana-chan,
our sweethearts!

203
00:11:13,560 --> 00:11:15,840
When it's a senior's idea, I'm against it.

204
00:11:15,840 --> 00:11:20,680
You, raised in New York, couldn't understand this shitamachi-style greeting.
Now back off!

205
00:11:22,700 --> 00:11:24,960
Really? Do whatever you want, then.

206
00:11:25,420 --> 00:11:27,860
Hah, don't you dare enjoy yourself alone!

207
00:11:30,200 --> 00:11:32,100
Everyone, this is ridiculous.

208
00:11:32,980 --> 00:11:34,660
Aren't you going, big brother?

209
00:11:38,860 --> 00:11:39,420
Eek!

210
00:11:40,080 --> 00:11:40,960
Eek!

211
00:11:41,200 --> 00:11:43,840
My heart's pounding.

212
00:11:44,020 --> 00:11:44,420
Let's go.

213
00:11:44,760 --> 00:11:45,720
Excuse us!

214
00:11:46,960 --> 00:11:48,260
Wh-wh-whoa!

215
00:11:50,820 --> 00:11:52,020
There's nobody here.

216
00:11:52,280 --> 00:11:53,000
Ryo-chan.

217
00:11:56,040 --> 00:11:57,420
I knew you'd come.

218
00:11:57,420 --> 00:12:00,500
Gross! You guys, don't get in the
bath with towels wrapped around you!

219
00:12:01,140 --> 00:12:02,220
Ladies!

220
00:12:02,220 --> 00:12:03,620
No, wait, Yose, hold on a second!

221
00:12:04,100 --> 00:12:04,720
Yaah!

222
00:12:20,440 --> 00:12:21,660
Do you need something?

223
00:12:24,460 --> 00:12:25,560
Just as I thought.

224
00:12:25,560 --> 00:12:26,640
Kōkishii!

225
00:12:29,120 --> 00:12:30,460
Kōkishii!

226
00:12:30,460 --> 00:12:31,160
What is it?

227
00:12:34,940 --> 00:12:36,080
Kōkishii!

228
00:12:36,080 --> 00:12:36,880
Please stop.

229
00:12:37,740 --> 00:12:40,040
Nakagawa, you have that kind of hobby...

230
00:12:40,040 --> 00:12:41,280
That's not true.

231
00:12:41,280 --> 00:12:41,920
Kōkishii!

232
00:12:41,920 --> 00:12:43,240
Kōkishii!

233
00:12:45,280 --> 00:12:46,460
What's wrong?

234
00:12:46,960 --> 00:12:48,100
Pull yourself together, please.

235
00:12:48,100 --> 00:12:50,120
Pull yourself together, please.

236
00:12:51,660 --> 00:12:53,500
What we're doing makes no sense.

237
00:13:14,260 --> 00:13:20,820
He seems to have calmed down, but if his blood pressure goes up again, it's very dangerous.
Whatever you do, don't get him excited.

238
00:13:22,200 --> 00:13:24,780
I'll come check on him later.
Take care of yourself.

239
00:13:25,980 --> 00:13:31,780
Honestly, these New York-raised kids these days,
look away for a second and there's no telling what they'll pull.

240
00:13:31,780 --> 00:13:32,960
Hey, Volvo.

241
00:13:35,300 --> 00:13:38,380
Could you not shout in front of a sick man?

242
00:13:38,380 --> 00:13:39,780
Hey, Honda-san.

243
00:13:40,140 --> 00:13:40,500
Yes?

244
00:13:45,080 --> 00:13:49,200
Tayama's old man seemed pretty healthy
when he came to the bathhouse, though.

245
00:13:50,300 --> 00:13:52,120
What on earth happened?

246
00:13:52,120 --> 00:13:55,820
The moment he saw my face,
he called me Mitsuyoshi, and then...

247
00:13:55,820 --> 00:13:58,880
Mitsuyoshi... I see.

248
00:13:59,260 --> 00:14:02,120
When I saw you,
I thought you looked like someone, too.

249
00:14:02,120 --> 00:14:03,760
Who's this Mitsuyoshi you're talking about?

250
00:14:04,420 --> 00:14:06,620
Tayama's old man's one and only son.

251
00:14:06,620 --> 00:14:07,520
Son?

252
00:14:07,980 --> 00:14:09,240
There it is. Found it.

253
00:14:12,620 --> 00:14:14,420
He looks just like Nakagawa, doesn't he?

254
00:14:14,800 --> 00:14:18,340
Old man Tayama used to
be a skilled carpenter.

255
00:14:19,760 --> 00:14:21,980
But with the times changing,
the work dried up,

256
00:14:21,980 --> 00:14:23,940
and he started drinking heavily.

257
00:14:23,940 --> 00:14:26,660
And on top of that, over whether
to take over the business or not,

258
00:14:26,660 --> 00:14:28,900
he had a huge fight with his only son,
Kokichi.

259
00:14:29,680 --> 00:14:31,480
I never got to see what you were capable of.

260
00:14:31,900 --> 00:14:33,300
He never said where he was going.

261
00:14:36,580 --> 00:14:39,100
He didn't even show up
at his mother's funeral.

262
00:14:39,100 --> 00:14:41,380
I wonder where he is
and what he's doing now.

263
00:14:42,680 --> 00:14:46,460
So you saw Nakagawa and
thought the son had come back?

264
00:14:47,180 --> 00:14:48,820
With him looking this much like him,
no wonder.

265
00:14:49,200 --> 00:14:51,520
He must have been so happy
his blood pressure shot up.

266
00:14:53,460 --> 00:14:55,440
He used to be a stubborn,
quarrelsome old man,

267
00:14:55,440 --> 00:14:57,920
but lately he's gone completely timid.

268
00:14:59,240 --> 00:15:00,120
Somehow, I...

269
00:15:00,700 --> 00:15:03,120
feel like I've done something terrible.

270
00:15:04,860 --> 00:15:08,620
This might be the perfect chance
to cut Nakagawa down to size.

271
00:15:09,100 --> 00:15:10,300
If it turns out to be a
case of mistaken identity,

272
00:15:10,620 --> 00:15:12,380
the old man is going to be so disappointed.

273
00:15:14,400 --> 00:15:15,460
Looks like he's come to.

274
00:15:15,460 --> 00:15:16,960
W-what should we do?

275
00:15:18,220 --> 00:15:20,120
Where are we?

276
00:15:20,120 --> 00:15:21,740
Thank goodness, old man.

277
00:15:21,740 --> 00:15:24,820
Your precious son Mitsuyoshi has come home!

278
00:15:24,820 --> 00:15:26,560
Senpai Mitsuyoshi!

279
00:15:26,560 --> 00:15:27,940
Mitsuyoshi...

280
00:15:27,940 --> 00:15:28,940
I'm...

281
00:15:28,940 --> 00:15:30,700
Glad you're back, Mitsuyoshi.

282
00:15:30,700 --> 00:15:33,900
After all these years, finally reunited
with the father you longed to see.

283
00:15:33,900 --> 00:15:35,180
Mitsuyoshi...

284
00:15:37,180 --> 00:15:39,940
Well then, leave you two to
enjoy some quality father-son time.

285
00:15:39,940 --> 00:15:41,260
Let's make ourselves scarce.

286
00:15:41,260 --> 00:15:42,660
Are you sure, Ryo-san?

287
00:15:42,660 --> 00:15:43,300
But...

288
00:15:43,300 --> 00:15:44,900
No, no, come on, come on!

289
00:15:44,900 --> 00:15:45,740
Senpai.

290
00:15:47,980 --> 00:15:50,260
You still have the look of defeat in your eyes,
don't you?

291
00:15:53,420 --> 00:15:56,100
Dad, and Senior Ryotsu, who looked after us,

292
00:15:56,100 --> 00:15:57,160
please do stay the night

293
00:15:57,160 --> 00:15:59,980
so we can repay your kindness,
in a small way.

294
00:16:00,460 --> 00:16:01,440
I see. I see.

295
00:16:01,440 --> 00:16:04,880
We live as you see, so we can't offer
much in the way of fine hospitality,

296
00:16:04,880 --> 00:16:06,300
but please take your time.

297
00:16:06,300 --> 00:16:09,320
No, that's not what I meant at all.

298
00:16:09,700 --> 00:16:11,820
If we let our son's benefactor
die right here before us,

299
00:16:11,820 --> 00:16:13,940
I'd have no face to show my late wife.

300
00:16:13,940 --> 00:16:16,080
Well, we'll be taking our leave.

301
00:16:17,960 --> 00:16:19,040
Don't run away! Hey!

302
00:16:19,220 --> 00:16:19,560
Wait!

303
00:16:24,680 --> 00:16:28,660
The bed's free too, so please,
take your time, Senior.

304
00:16:35,020 --> 00:16:38,180
Sorry I'm not much of a host.
If you get thirsty,

305
00:16:40,340 --> 00:16:41,060
Thank you, I'll have some.

306
00:16:44,840 --> 00:16:45,840
What is this?!

307
00:16:45,840 --> 00:16:45,960
This!

308
00:16:46,140 --> 00:16:51,360
Isn't this Mitsuyoshi's favorite, the special
bancha mixed with natto, miso, and sugar?

309
00:16:51,360 --> 00:16:52,380
Ugh...

310
00:16:53,280 --> 00:16:55,080
Maybe I didn't put in enough natto.

311
00:16:55,080 --> 00:16:57,220
I see, Mitsuyoshi's

312
00:17:01,440 --> 00:17:03,800
It's delicious, it really is.

313
00:17:03,800 --> 00:17:05,487
As for other food,

314
00:17:05,537 --> 00:17:08,840
all I have is the
croquette I bought at lunch.

315
00:17:08,840 --> 00:17:12,020
That looks delicious.
Since you're offering, I'll take one.

316
00:17:14,940 --> 00:17:17,130
Mitsuyoshi stretched out the croquette,

317
00:17:17,180 --> 00:17:20,740
you always liked pouring on so much
sauce that it turned pitch black.

318
00:17:20,800 --> 00:17:21,900
No, just as it is.

319
00:17:22,060 --> 00:17:24,620
Since we're at it, don't be stingy.
Have the whole thing.

320
00:17:26,580 --> 00:17:28,500
Go ahead and eat, Mitsuyoshi.

321
00:17:30,460 --> 00:17:31,860
Wow, that looks delicious.

322
00:17:38,520 --> 00:17:39,980
This is delicious.

323
00:17:43,900 --> 00:17:44,780
Delicious.

324
00:17:44,780 --> 00:17:48,560
It wouldn't be right to eat such
delicious food all by myself.

325
00:17:48,560 --> 00:17:49,820
Please, senior, have some too.

326
00:17:49,820 --> 00:17:50,980
No, I'm fine.

327
00:17:50,980 --> 00:17:52,940
Oh right, senior is a spicy food lover.

328
00:17:52,940 --> 00:17:55,040
Pass the chili pepper shaker.

329
00:17:55,040 --> 00:17:57,500
Hey, that one doesn't have its inner lid on.

330
00:17:58,660 --> 00:18:01,660
It's just the spiciness you like, senior.

331
00:18:01,660 --> 00:18:04,040
Who'd be happy with something like this?

332
00:18:04,720 --> 00:18:08,020
Nowadays, meeting a spirited
young fellow like you is rare.

333
00:18:09,980 --> 00:18:13,880
An only child like me would never say he couldn't do a thing,
not even if his mouth split open.

334
00:18:14,400 --> 00:18:15,320
Let's eat.

335
00:18:29,540 --> 00:18:31,560
Damn those buddies of mine!

336
00:18:32,000 --> 00:18:35,160
So, Kokichi,
you've become a police officer too?

337
00:18:35,160 --> 00:18:36,060
Well, yeah.

338
00:18:36,420 --> 00:18:39,640
So Kokichi became a policeman.

339
00:18:40,240 --> 00:18:46,220
I was so worried that you'd gone
astray and were up to no good somewhere.

340
00:19:06,200 --> 00:19:08,680
Senpai, you're still awake?

341
00:19:10,520 --> 00:19:15,160
We came all the way out here just because we
were too stubborn to back down to you, Senpai.

342
00:19:15,980 --> 00:19:18,420
We're doing a good thing here, right?

343
00:19:18,420 --> 00:19:23,480
I was the same, you know. I had a fight with my
old man once and ran off from the tsukudani shop.

344
00:19:24,460 --> 00:19:28,720
I couldn't help wondering if that
stubborn old man ever got lonely too.

345
00:19:30,440 --> 00:19:36,020
I've only ever had
misunderstandings with my father, too.

346
00:19:36,540 --> 00:19:40,940
So you've never even had
a proper father-son fight?

347
00:19:41,560 --> 00:19:41,960
Yeah.

348
00:19:42,860 --> 00:19:45,300
Your family's pretty strange too.

349
00:19:47,180 --> 00:19:49,480
What do we do from tomorrow, Senpai?

350
00:19:49,480 --> 00:19:52,860
Well, we've got no choice but to
keep going like this for a while.

351
00:19:54,520 --> 00:19:55,220
One more game!

352
00:19:55,820 --> 00:19:58,800
I give up. You really are strong, Father.

353
00:19:58,800 --> 00:20:01,140
I don't stand a chance against you.

354
00:20:01,140 --> 00:20:01,701
Kankichi,

355
00:20:01,751 --> 00:20:06,640
You've gotten awfully refined in
how you speak since we last met.

356
00:20:07,820 --> 00:20:10,440
I suppose Kankichi has grown up, too.

357
00:20:11,040 --> 00:20:12,972
You used to call me a goddamn old bastard,

358
00:20:13,022 --> 00:20:16,280
and you'd always snap back that
I was a stubborn old geezer.

359
00:20:16,280 --> 00:20:18,600
A stubborn old geezer?

360
00:20:18,800 --> 00:20:22,640
Somehow, the Kankichi I see
now feels so formal and distant.

361
00:20:23,020 --> 00:20:27,660
Is it really true that even a real father and son
become like strangers after being apart too long?

362
00:20:29,540 --> 00:20:30,200
Sorry.

363
00:20:31,140 --> 00:20:31,940
Actually, I...

364
00:20:31,940 --> 00:20:34,080
Kōkujī-kun, excuse us for a moment.

365
00:20:34,920 --> 00:20:37,320
The doctor said excitement is forbidden,
didn't he?

366
00:20:37,320 --> 00:20:40,000
If we tell him the truth and his
blood pressure shoots up again...

367
00:20:40,000 --> 00:20:42,300
This time,
who knows what might happen to the old man?

368
00:20:42,900 --> 00:20:46,260
Senpai, I can't keep
deceiving Mr. Tayama any longer.

369
00:20:46,260 --> 00:20:49,740
Stick with it. On top of pretending
to be some stranger's old man's son...

370
00:20:49,740 --> 00:20:52,040
If it gets out, we're finished.
We'll be fired!

371
00:20:52,740 --> 00:20:53,360
Pops.

372
00:20:54,860 --> 00:20:56,700
What's with that gloomy face

373
00:20:57,240 --> 00:20:59,340
Let's go soak in the bath and freshen up.

374
00:21:01,140 --> 00:21:02,940
Your way of talking hasn't
changed a bit from the old days!

375
00:21:03,440 --> 00:21:04,760
Don't be ridiculous, you blockhead!

376
00:21:04,960 --> 00:21:06,200
That's right, a true Edo-born man!

377
00:21:07,400 --> 00:21:09,240
I'm still not losing to
some young whippersnapper!

378
00:21:09,400 --> 00:21:11,060
Get lost, you hear!

379
00:21:15,440 --> 00:21:17,340
Well, if it isn't Tayama.

380
00:21:17,800 --> 00:21:19,320
You're looking spry as ever, aren't you?

381
00:21:19,560 --> 00:21:21,060
I'm in a good mood today.

382
00:21:27,540 --> 00:21:28,960
What a fine evening.

383
00:21:29,460 --> 00:21:32,500
I've got no regrets,
I could die any day now.

384
00:21:32,500 --> 00:21:33,960
What are you going on about, you fool?

385
00:21:33,960 --> 00:21:37,240
A stubborn old geezer like me
isn't kicking the bucket that easily!

386
00:21:37,240 --> 00:21:37,900
What's that supposed to mean?

387
00:21:45,920 --> 00:21:47,860
Growing up in the old downtown wears you out,
doesn't it?

388
00:21:55,160 --> 00:21:56,620
What is it, Mitsuyoshi?

389
00:21:56,620 --> 00:21:59,340
Mitsuyoshi, you go into the bath
with a towel wrapped around you?

390
00:22:00,240 --> 00:22:01,252
Brings back memories.

391
00:22:01,302 --> 00:22:05,400
Whenever you came to the bathhouse,
you always swung it around with such gusto.

392
00:22:06,140 --> 00:22:08,680
Kou-chan, look! Cool, cool!

393
00:22:09,540 --> 00:22:11,080
Cool, cool...

394
00:22:11,500 --> 00:22:14,100
Show me that again, it's been a while.
Hey, Mitsuyoshi.

395
00:22:14,900 --> 00:22:15,540
No good?

396
00:22:15,780 --> 00:22:17,360
I-I see.

397
00:22:26,620 --> 00:22:31,560
You're still green, all talk and no substance.
You don't know the spirit of the town.

398
00:22:40,920 --> 00:22:44,300
Hey, this is strange.

399
00:22:46,240 --> 00:22:50,140
Calm down, you're still alive, this one.

400
00:22:56,940 --> 00:22:59,600
Mitsuyoshi, when did you get here?

401
00:22:59,940 --> 00:23:02,020
This one's the real Mitsuyoshi.

402
00:23:02,500 --> 00:23:04,260
Dad, I'm sorry.

403
00:23:05,660 --> 00:23:08,560
Mitsuyoshi, Mitsuyoshi!

404
00:23:09,400 --> 00:23:12,680
Dad, they said we could go
home once we throw it down...

405
00:23:12,680 --> 00:23:15,280
But your fever's still going up

406
00:23:16,360 --> 00:23:17,520
But he was a bit off.

407
00:23:17,520 --> 00:23:18,923
Doing something like that...

408
00:23:18,973 --> 00:23:21,880
You're in your right mind, you know. I, I...

409
00:23:22,220 --> 00:23:25,080
Good for you, old man. Good, good.

410
00:23:26,800 --> 00:23:27,580
Go on, go!

411
00:23:27,700 --> 00:23:28,040
Yes!

412
00:23:30,280 --> 00:23:31,840
Dad! Look, look!

413
00:23:32,920 --> 00:23:37,360
Round and round and round! Look, look!

414
00:23:38,540 --> 00:23:40,740
Then who on earth was that?

415
00:23:42,020 --> 00:23:42,960
The real one?

416
00:23:44,200 --> 00:23:45,400
Well, never mind.

417
00:23:45,400 --> 00:23:47,680
Are you watching, Dad? Look, look!

418
00:23:48,060 --> 00:23:51,620
The Nagakawa towel that even
we couldn't snatch by force,

419
00:23:51,620 --> 00:23:55,580
was taken so easily by that
old man's sincere heart.

420
00:23:56,620 --> 00:24:00,700
Isn't that a sunny, heartwarming story?
The whole shitamachi is full of it!

421
00:24:04,740 --> 00:24:15,080
There he goes again, the outrageous professor! This time he's on the moon.
Why do I have to keep going to space on an island with you?

422
00:24:15,640 --> 00:24:21,940
Next time: a story that's no story. Mass-produced Eiku,
Japan edition, see you then!

423
00:24:37,660 --> 00:24:44,140
Sweet, with
"tokiai," resolved quickly, helping out swiftly.

424
00:24:44,140 --> 00:24:55,680
Decided, flash of inspiration, bouncing along,
wrapping up, taking action, flying off.

425
00:24:56,580 --> 00:25:00,360
Above all, the amazing power.

426
00:25:00,360 --> 00:25:12,640
Everyone gather! Come here,
and you'll find the dreamlike final energy.

427
00:25:13,740 --> 00:25:23,720
Gaze at tomorrow, believe in yesterday, paint the universe,
stand on the ground, and the star of Kameari will come.

428
00:25:25,940 --> 00:25:29,000
This'll do, right? As if it would!

429
00:25:42,320 --> 00:25:43,720
Thank you for watching.

